SUMMARY:Chipper's Preschool & Sensory Skate
DESCRIPTION:Get some morning wiggles out at Oaks Park Roller Rink where kiddos can skate at their own pace during their special toddler skate time on Tuesdays and Wednesdays from 10 AM-11:30 AM. \nEnjoy skating fun\, snack time\, and a visit with Chipper the Squirrel. As part of this specialty session\, Coach Amy teaches a 15-minute group skating lesson that introduces young kids to the principles of body movement while helping toddlers learn to follow directions through fun games. \nSensory Skate\nNow offering a special sensory-sensitive skate time during the Wednesday Preschool Skate. Music volumes will be reduced\, disco lights turned off\, and a quiet sensory play space will be provided. Sensory Skate is open to all children 10 and younger and their families.
URL:https://pdxparent.com/event-single/chippers-preschool-sensory-skate/2026-03-18/
LOCATION:Oaks Amusement Park\, 7805 SE Oaks Park Way\, Portland\, OR\, 97202
CATEGORIES:Active,Kids Calendar
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://pdxparent.com/wp-content/uploads/preschool-skate-oaks-park-1.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Pdx Parent": "https://pdxparent.com/event-single/enduring-impressions-contemporary-woodblock-prints/2026-03-18/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pdx_parent
X-SOURCE:Pdx Parent
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260318T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260318T153000
DTSTAMP:20260317T230600
CREATED:20260219T221804Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260219T221843Z
UID:10054579-1773828000-1773847800@pdxparent.com
SUMMARY:Enduring Impressions: Contemporary Woodblock Prints
DESCRIPTION:Step into a world where nature-themed prints meet Portland Japanese Garden’s springtime vibrance in Enduring Impressions: Contemporary Woodblock Prints. Featuring the art of mokuhanga (木版画)\, Japanese-style woodblock printmaking\, this exhibition reveals how a centuries-old tradition is experiencing a contemporary revival as artists around the world use the quiet power and unique characteristics of woodblock printmaking to create captivating works of art. \nMokuhanga has been embraced as an environmentally friendly art form that uses wood\, water-based pigments\, and paper made from plant fibers. The exhibition’s featured artists are among the growing international movement where meticulously crafted art prints incorporating these traditional tools and techniques are complemented by alternative printmaking technologies and strategies for contemporary expression. This exhibition marks the Garden’s first collaboration with the Honolulu Museum of Art and is co-curated by Stephen Salel\, the Museum’s Curator of Japanese Art. Across the galleries at Portland Japanese Garden\, Enduring Impressions presents an eclectic range of contemporary prints\, alongside a behind-the-scenes look at the process\, history and future of this iconic art form. \nEditor’s note: This event is a community submission.
URL:https://pdxparent.com/event-single/enduring-impressions-contemporary-woodblock-prints/2026-03-18/
LOCATION:Portland Japanese Garden\, 611 SW Kingston Ave.\, Portland\, OR\, 97205
CATEGORIES:Arts/Crafts,Kids Calendar,Plants & Nature
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://pdxparent.com/wp-content/uploads/PortlandJapaneseGarden_EnduringImpressions_KeyVisual.jpg
END:VEVENT
