BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:friends_of_trees_green_space
X-SOURCE:Friends Of Trees Green Space
DTSTART:20260320T164500Z
DTEND:20260320T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T060605Z
UID:523t42t152kag5ufa02vgoe468@google.com
CREATED:20260303T232851Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><b>Help needed to plant hundreds of native trees and shrubs 
 at Gateway Green at this rare Friday event! </b>This event was originally s
 cheduled for Sat\, Feb 21st and canceled due to strong wind gusts onsite --
  please help make it possible to give these plants a new home at this this 
 unique mountain-biking and walking oasis situated in between I-84 and I-205
 . </p><p><em>This park is only accessible via the I-205 Multi-Use Path. The
 re is an approximately 15 minute walk from the former Kohl's parking lot do
 wn the multi-use path to our planting site\, look for our signs. Volunteers
  are encouraged to bike to the planting or take public transportation to th
 e transit center and walk from there.</em></p><p>Please arrive by 9:45am to
  sign-in and be assigned a planting crew. The planting starts at 10:00am. W
 e provide gloves\, tools\, and planting guidance\, as well as breakfast sna
 cks and coffee/tea/hot chocolate -- all you need to do is show up dressed f
 or the weather wearing sturdy shoes or boots\, and be ready to have fun!</p
 ><p><b>How do I register? </b>Register by filling out <b><a href="https://w
 ww.tfaforms.com/4840511?tfa_26=a0TPa00001KeKh6&tfa_2189=Gateway%20Green%20p
 lanting\,%20NE%20Portland&tfa_31=a0VPa00000G41lu&tfa_45=Tree%20Planter\,%20
 %20at%20March%2020\,%202026%20at%209:45%20am&tfa_2190=2026-03-20&tfa_49=3.2
 5&tfa_886=Standard%20FOT&tfa_51=offsite" target="_blank"><u>this quick form
 </u></a></b>.  Groups\, families\, and individuals welcome!</p><p><b>Under 
 age 18?</b> We request that youth 15 and under volunteer with a parent/guar
 dian.  Youth 16 and older can volunteer on their own and will need to hand 
 us a <b><u><a href="http://friendsoftrees.org/youthwaiver" target="_blank">
 <u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>you
 th waiver form</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u><
 /u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a></u></b> signed by their parent/guar
 dian.</p><p><b>Questions?  </b>Pl<u></u>ease check out our <a href="https:/
 /friendsoftrees.org/volunteer-faq/" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u
 ><u><u><u><u><b><u>Volunteer FAQ webpage</u></b></u></u></u></u></u></u></u
 ></u></u></u></u></u></a>.  Our team is also happy to assist! <a href="mail
 to:Volunteer@friendsoftrees.org" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u
 ><u><u><u><b><u>volunteer@fr<u></u>iendsoftrees.or<u></u>g</u></b></u></u><
 /u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a> / 503-595-0213 We look forward 
 to working together soon!<br></p><p>===</p><p>Thank you to our event sponso
 r\, <a href="https://wyldcanna.com/" target="_blank"><u><u><u>WYLD</u></u><
 /u></a>.</p><p>===</p><b><hr /></b><p>This event in partnership with Portla
 nd Parks &amp\; Recreation and Oregon Department of Forestry. </p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260303T233232Z
LOCATION:10010 NE Halsey St\, Portland\, OR 97220\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Friday Gateway Green planting (NE Portland\, OR)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
