SUMMARY:Eid at the Bon!
DESCRIPTION:Chef James Moody has prepared a feast with special halal lamb
  to celebrate Eid al-Fitr\, marking the end of Ramadan.&#160\;  All are w
 elcome to feast on this special meal.&#160\;  Menu:Main DishesSpiced Lamb
  Pilaf (Halal)        Aromatic basmati rice layered with tender lamb\, wa
 rm spices\, herbs\, and caramelized onions.      Herb‑Roasted Tofu &amp
 \; Vegetable Pilaf        A plant‑forward pilaf with seasoned tofu\, to
 matoes\, herbs\, and fragrant rice.      Oven‑Roasted Herb Potatoes    
     Golden potatoes tossed with herbs and sea salt.      Slow‑Braised S
 easonal Cabbage        Gently stewed cabbage with garlic and Mediterranea
 n spices.      Roasted Cauliflower with Sumac        Lightly charred flor
 ets seasoned with sumac and fresh herbs.      SaladMediterranean Kachumbe
 r‑Style Salad        A refreshing diced salad of fresh vegetables with 
 citrus and mint.      AccompanimentsSweet Mango &amp\; Red Pepper Relish 
        A lightly spiced mango garnish with a sweet‑heat balance.      M
 int &amp\; Cucumber Yogurt        Cool\, creamy yogurt with herbs and cuc
 umber        With gratitude to Chef Moody and the Bon Appetit staff. Plea
 se note the adjusted closing hour of 7pm due to the commencement of Sprin
 g Break.  Thank you!
