BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:friends_of_trees_neighborhood
X-SOURCE:Friends Of Trees Neighborhood
DTSTART:20260321T154500Z
DTEND:20260321T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T060606Z
UID:6ot8b3lkkeb21lisl60u75cfpg@google.com
CREATED:20250820T225010Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>=======</p><p><b>Due to popular interest\, this event is <u>
 full and closed</u></b>. Please consider supporting any other open event --
  we hope to work with you soon!</p><p>=======</p><p>Let's plant trees toget
 her in East Portland!  Interested in receiving a tree? Click <b><u><a href=
 "https://friendsoftrees.org/get-a-tree/" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u>
 <u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>HERE</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u>
 </u></u></u></u></a></u></b> to purchase a tree for your household. Dozens 
 of large (6-10' tall) trees will be ready for planting in their new homes\,
  and your help is what makes this community planting possible!</p><p>Please
  arrive by 8:45am to sign-in and be assigned a planting crew. The planting 
 starts at 9:00am. We provide gloves\, tools\, and guidance\, as well as lig
 ht breakfast snacks and coffee/tea/hot chocolate. We ask that all volunteer
 s dress for the weather\, wear sturdy shoes/boots you don't mind getting di
 rty\, and be ready to have fun!</p><p><b>Under age 18?</b> We request that 
 youth 15 and under volunteer with a parent/guardian.  Youth 16 and older ca
 n volunteer on their own and will need to hand us a <b><u><a href="http://f
 riendsoftrees.org/youthwaiver" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><
 u><u><u><u><u><u>youth waiver form</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u><
 /u></u></u></u></u></a></u></b> signed by their parent/guardian.</p><p><b>P
 rivate transportation</b>: You will travel from the meeting location to a f
 ew planting sites in the nearby neighborhood (up to several miles). <b>We r
 ecommend private transportation</b> (bike or vehicle)\, but there may be an
  option to carpool if others in your small planting crew are also comfortab
 le with this. </p><p><b>Questions?  </b>Pl<u></u>ease check out our <a href
 ="https://friendsoftrees.org/volunteer-faq/" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u
 ><u><u><u><u><u><u><b><u>Volunteer FAQ webpage</u></b></u></u></u></u></u><
 /u></u></u></u></u></u></a>.  Our team is also happy to assist! <a href="ma
 ilto:Volunteer@friendsoftrees.org" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>
 <u><u><u><b><u>volunteer@fr<u></u>iendsoftrees.or<u></u>g</u></b></u></u></
 u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a> / 503-595-0213 We look forward to wo
 rking together soon!<br></p><p><b>What neighborhoods will the trees be plan
 ted in?</b> Argay Terrace\, Hazelwood\, Parkrose\, Parkrose Heights\, Russe
 ll\, and Wilkes.</p><p>Thank you to our event sponsors <a href="https://www
 .nba.com/blazers/" target="_blank"><u>Portland Trail Blazers</u></a> and <a
  href="https://northamerica.daimlertruck.com/" target="_blank"><u>Daimler T
 ruck North America</u></a>.</p><b><hr /></b><p></p><p>This event in partner
 ship with Portland Urban Forestry.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260317T233001Z
LOCATION:Level Beer\, 5211 NE 148th Ave\, Portland\, OR 97230\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
