SUMMARY:Getting Ready on the Inside: Emotional Emergency Prep for Families
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T210000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260321T223000Z
UID:698e49d6491b809c6f196da5@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Talking with children about emergencies can feel overwhelming.
  This workshop offers a trauma-informed approach to emergency preparedness
  that centers family strengths\, community connections\, and imagination. 
 Families will work together to create simple “pocket plans” using the 
 resources they already have.\nThis program is part of Hillsboro Reads.
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Brookwood
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698e49d6491b809c6f196da5
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
