X-SOURCE:Meetup Portland City Walking
UID:event_313734803@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260318T060609Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260325T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260325T123000
SUMMARY:Bull Mountain Urban‑Wild Hills Challenge
DESCRIPTION:Portland City Trail Walking Group\n**7.5 miles**\n\\*\\*\\~900–1000 ft gain \\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*Stretch your legs and lungs on this surprisingly hilly loop right in Tigard’s backyard. We’ll start from an easy on‑street parking area near Sunrise Park and quickly leave the cars behind for a mix of quiet neighborhood streets and hidden green spaces. \\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*Our route links together the forested Ascension Trail\, the meadows and singletrack of Cach Natural Area\, and a steady climb to the Bull Mountain high point on High Tor Drive\, with views toward the valley on a clear day. Expect multiple shorter climbs rather than one big grind\, plus a nice blend of pavement and real trail underfoot. \\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*This is an ideal “training hike” for longer spring and summer adventures: about 7.5 miles with roughly 900–1000 feet of elevation gain\, at a social but steady pace. Most of the hike is within neighborhoods\, but there are several stretches of true wooded trail where it feels surprisingly wild for being so close to home. \\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*Recommended: sturdy walking shoes or light hikers\, water\, and layers for changing weather. Poles are optional but can be handy on the steeper ups and downs. \\*\\*\n\n3/4/26 Update - I checked the trail after last night's hard rain. There are several spots on the trail that are very muddy. I highly recommend boots and encourage the use of treking poles if you have them for the steep sections.\n\nRoute map: https://www.alltrails.com/explore/recording/afternoon-hike-e2ad92e
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/portland-city-walking-and-trail-walking-meetup-group/events/313734803/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260310T231448Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260310T231448Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/3/7/2/f/600_531914127.jpeg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lan Su Garden": "https://lansugarden.org/event/magnolia-floral-showcase/2026-03-25/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lan_su_garden
X-SOURCE:Lan Su Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260325T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260325T183000
DTSTAMP:20260316T230050
CREATED:20260312T013728Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260312T014055Z
UID:10000872-1774432800-1774463400@lansugarden.org
SUMMARY:Magnolia Floral Showcase
DESCRIPTION:March 20-30\, 2026 \n\n\n\nFind inspiration and moments of pure beauty in a wonderland of flowers! Enjoy large-scale magnolia installations throughout the garden\, along with interpretive displays featuring educational posters\, huayi floral pieces\, and a magnolia penjing.   \n\n\n\nOur featured floral artist\, Lauren Say\, is a past participant in our Chrysanthemum Festival Floral Design Showcase. In 2025\, her design “Seasonal Suspense” took second place in the People’s Choice Awards and third prize from the judges. Come see how she transforms the new flower of the season into works of art!  \n\n\n\nLan Su’s own horticulture team will complete the showcase with their artistic takes on magnolias in floral design.   \n\n\n\nThe Magnolia Floral Showcase is free with admission or membership\, so grab a friend and come explore!  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAdmission Rates\n\n\n\n\nLan Su Members & Guests: FREE\n\n\n\nAdult: $16.95\n\n\n\nSenior (62+) or Student (18+ with ID): $15.95\n\n\n\nYouth (6-18 yr): $13.95\n\n\n\nChild (5 yr & under): FREE\n\n\n\n\nNote: A $0.95 service fee is reflected in each paid admission. \n\n\n\nDiscounted Admission Offers\n\n\n\nThese offers must be redeemed in person at the Lan Su Ticket Booth to confirm eligibility. \n\n\n\nEBT/WIC Cardholders\n\n\n\nDiscounted admission of $5.00 per person is available for up to four individuals per EBT/WIC card. To claim this offer\, please present your EBT/WIC card and a valid form of photo ID at the Ticket Booth. \n\n\n\nVeterans & Military\n\n\n\nWe offer $2 off admission for active-duty military\, veterans\, and their immediate family members with valid ID. The discount must be redeemed in person at the Ticket Booth. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nParking & Directions\n\n\n\nFree Lan Su Parking\n\n\n\nThere is free first come\, first served parking in our sister lot next to the garden at 424 NW Third Avenue. Additional metered parking and garages are available on surrounding streets.
URL:https://lansugarden.org/event/magnolia-floral-showcase/2026-03-25/
LOCATION:Lan Su Chinese Garden\, 239 NW Everett Street\, Portland\, Oregon\, 97209
CATEGORIES:Art,Free with admission or membership,Horticulture,Magnolia Festival
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://lansugarden.org/wp-content/uploads/lauren-say-floral-design-1200x800-1.webp
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lan Su Garden": "https://lansugarden.org/event/plant-wednesday-spotlight/2026-03-25/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lan_su_garden
X-SOURCE:Lan Su Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260325T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260325T113000
DTSTAMP:20260316T230050
CREATED:20250819T214828Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260220T232114Z
UID:10000761-1774436400-1774438200@lansugarden.org
SUMMARY:#PlantWednesday Spotlight
DESCRIPTION:Join our horticulture team every Wednesday for a tour diving into a plant in its peak\, gardening tips\, and more. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWednesdays\, 11-11:30 AM | Free with admission or membership \n\n\n\nThe #PlantWednesday Spotlight is a unique “show & tell” program featuring different captivating topics every month. Meet Lan Su’s horticulture team each Wednesday to explore\, learn\, and connect with the natural beauty of Lan Su. These are short 30-min sessions that showcase a horticultural wonder\, technique\, or tool that our passionate horticulturists want to share with fellow plant enthusiasts. Each session will shine a light on the behind-the-scenes operations of the garden\, highlight a plant at its peak beauty\, or focus on recent improvements to our collection. \n\n\n\nEach session will explore a different part of the garden based on that week’s topic. When you arrive\, please check in with the front door staff or volunteers for the exact location to meet in. \n\n\n\n\nGet Admission\n\n\n\n\nThis program is FREE with garden admission or membership. No registration needed.
URL:https://lansugarden.org/event/plant-wednesday-spotlight/2026-03-25/
LOCATION:Lan Su Chinese Garden\, 239 NW Everett Street\, Portland\, Oregon\, 97209
CATEGORIES:Free with admission or membership,Horticulture,Tours
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://lansugarden.org/wp-content/uploads/PlantWednesday-Spotlight-hidden-garden.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Lan Su Chinese Garden":MAILTO:info@lansugarden.org
END:VEVENT
