UID:10000842-1774702800-1774706400@lansugarden.org
SUMMARY:Garden Tea Tastings with Hannah Ma (1 PM)
DESCRIPTION:Overview\n\n\n\nTickets\n\n\n\nTea Master\n\n\n\nParking & Directions\n\n\n\n\nSeries Overview\n\n\n\nThis spring\, take a front-row seat to Chinese tea culture with our intimate Garden Tea Tasting Series (March–May)\, led by tea master Hannah Ma. Savor three seasonal teas from Yun Shui Teahouse\, learn traditional brewing techniques\, and explore the stories behind centuries of tea culture. Your ticket includes admission to Lan Su Chinese Garden on the day of your tasting. \n\n\n\nAfter your 1-hour tasting\, you’ll receive a porcelain teacup to continue your journey at home. All sampled teas will also be available for purchase in our Yun Shui Teahouse. \n\n\n\nFull Series Schedule\n\n\n\nSaturdays & Sundays\, March 21–April 26 | 11:00 AM & 1:00 PM \n\n\n\nFridays & Sundays\, May 1–May 31 | 1:00 PM & 3:00 PM \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGet Tickets\n\n\n\nSeating is very limited for these intimate group tastings\, so reserve your seat early. Your ticket includes garden admission on the day of your tasting. \n\n\n\n\nLan Su Members & Guests: $36.95\n\n\n\nNon-Members: $55.95\n\n\n\n\nNote: A $0.95 service fee is reflected in each paid ticket \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMeet the Tea Master: Hannah Ma \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nA Portland native\, Hannah grew up drinking tea almost as often as water. Her passion was formally cultivated during her senior year of high school\, when she gained extensive experience with diverse tea blends and preparation techniques as a tea-rista at Portal Tea Company (formerly Tea Chai Té). Now a beverage enthusiast of more than six years\, Hannah is thrilled to join Lan Su’s Tea Tasting program\, where she shares science-based insights into tea’s properties and explores the rich traditions of Chinese-style tea ceremonies. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nParking & Directions\n\n\n\nFree Lan Su Parking\n\n\n\nThere is free first come\, first served parking in our sister lot next to the garden at 424 NW Third Avenue. Additional metered parking and garages are available on surrounding streets.
URL:https://lansugarden.org/event/garden-tea-tasting-1pm/2026-03-28/
LOCATION:Lan Su Chinese Garden\, 239 NW Everett Street\, Portland\, Oregon\, 97209
CATEGORIES:Tea
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://lansugarden.org/wp-content/uploads/garden-tea-tastings-hannah-ma-1200x800-1.webp
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Literary Arts": "https://literary-arts.org/event/with-abandon-toward-a-poetics-of-absence/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:literary_arts
X-SOURCE:Literary Arts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260328T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260328T170000
DTSTAMP:20260317T230545
CREATED:20260225T211129Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260311T220148Z
UID:10005653-1774702800-1774717200@literary-arts.org
SUMMARY:With Abandon: Toward a Poetics of Absence
DESCRIPTION:What remains in the wake of human industry and habitation? What comes after the end of a town\, a city\, an empire—or\, for that matter\, the death of a species\, an ecosystem\, a nation\, a language? And what happens to communities\, human and otherwise\, after they have been\, in a word\, abandoned?  \nThis four-hour masterclass will explore geographies and poems inscribed by such disappearances and afterlives. In the first half\, through close reading and discussion\, we will turn to an eclectic array of poets\, philosophers\, and thinkers—among them C.D. Wright\, Tyehimba Jess\, Samuel Amadon\, David Tomás Martinez\, Cathy Park Hong\, Martin Heidegger\, Abdelatif Laâbi\, Graham Harman\, and John Berger—whose works grapple with ruin\, memory\, and what persists.   \nThe second half will shift to generative writing\, with prompts applicable to both poetry and prose that invite participants to compose their own inquiries into what lingers\, what transforms\, and what new forms of life might emerge from sites of ending. \nAccess Program\nWe want our writing classes and seminars to be accessible to everyone\, regardless of income and background. We understand that our tuition structure can present obstacles for some people. Our Access Program offers writing class and seminar tuitions at a reduced rate. Most writing classes have at least one access spot available. \nPlease apply here for access rate tuition. Contact Susan Moore at susan@literary-arts.org if you have questions. \nLiaison position\nEvery in-person class and seminar at Literary Arts has one liaison position. Liaisons perform specific duties for each class meeting. If you are a liaison for a class or seminar\, the full amount of your tuition is covered by Literary Arts. \nApply here for the liaison position.
URL:https://literary-arts.org/event/with-abandon-toward-a-poetics-of-absence/
LOCATION:Literary Arts
CATEGORIES:Writing Classes,In-person
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://literary-arts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/1.jpg
GEO:45.5213897;-122.6810304
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
