BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Crystal Ballroom": "https://www.crystalballroompdx.com/events/272115-st-paul-the-broken-bones/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:crystal_ballroom
X-SOURCE:Crystal Ballroom
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260329T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260329T203000
DTSTAMP:20260317T230559
CREATED:20251002T233007Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251002T233011Z
UID:10000980-1774816200-1774816200@www.crystalballroompdx.com
SUMMARY:St Paul & The Broken Bones
DESCRIPTION:St. Paul & The Broken Bones are a powerhouse soul ensemble from Alabama known for their electrifying live shows and impassioned vocals. Formed in Birmingham in 2011\, the band features Paul Janeway (vocals)\, Jesse Phillips (bass)\, Browan Lollar (guitar)\, Kevin Leon (drums)\, Al Gamble (keyboards)\, Allen Branstetter (trumpet)\, Chad Fisher (trombone)\, and Amari Ansari (saxophone). \nTheir new self-titled sixth album marks a creative renewal-melding the band’s adventurous spirit with a return to soulful\, song-focused roots. Recorded at the legendary FAME Studios and produced by Eg White (Adele\, Celine Dion)\, the record blends psych-funk grooves\, gospel-tinged ballads\, and cinematic rock flourishes. Tracks like “Sushi and Coca-Cola” and “Going Back” reflect both personal introspection and the band’s deepened identity after a decade of evolution. \nSt. Paul & The Broken Bones have shared stages with The Rolling Stones\, Lizzo\, and Black Pumas\, and performed at major festivals like Coachella\, Glastonbury\, Lollapalooza\, and Bonnaroo. Even Sir Elton John took notice\, inviting them to perform at his Oscar party. Blending rock & roll\, soul\, R&B\, and more\, the band continues to captivate audiences around the world.
URL:https://www.crystalballroompdx.com/events/272115-st-paul-the-broken-bones/
CATEGORIES:March
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.crystalballroompdx.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/StPaul25-FVnvTZ.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wccls Library": "https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699522474dacf581ff7c0b4e"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wccls_library
SUMMARY:Makerspace Open Lab
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260329T203000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260330T003000Z
UID:699522474dacf581ff7c0b4e@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Makerspace Open Labs are for anyone who wants to check out the
  space and use our equipment to make cool things. Room assistants are avai
 lable to guide you in the basic use of the tools and technology. Come in w
 ith an idea and leave with a finished project! For more information about 
 the Makerspace and its resources\,\nsee here\n.\nMakerspace Open Labs take
  place on the following weekly schedule:\nTuesdays\n\, 5:30 - 7:30PM\nThur
 sdays\n\, 4:00 - 6:00PM\nSaturdays\n\, 10:00 AM - 1:00PM\nSundays\n\, 1:30
  - 5:30P\nEach month we provide the materials\, tools and instructions for
  a featured Makerspace project that everyone is invited to try.\nMarch's f
 eatured project is Recycled Shrinky Dink Jewelry (pictured).\nIMPORTANT:\n
 Adults using the Makerspace for the first time need to\nsign a waiver\n\; 
 people under the age of 18 must have a waiver signed by a parent or guardi
 an.\nYou can sign and submit waivers online here.
LOCATION:Tualatin Public Library\, Makerspace
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699522474dacf581ff7c0b4e
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
