SUMMARY:Digital Navigator One on One Tech Help
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260401T170000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260401T190000Z
UID:68f17e4861706d28001e1907@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Digital Navigator One-On-One Tech Help each Wednesday from 10:
 00 a.m. -12:00 p.m. in the library. Need help with digital questions or jo
 b searches? This free program is in partnership with American Connection C
 orps & The Washington County Cooperative Library Services. Call the librar
 y at 503 324-1382 to schedule a session.\nIf no appointments are scheduled
  drop in tech help will be available.\nThe Digital Navigator Program (DNP)
  is a free service made possible by a partnership\nbetween Washington Coun
 ty Cooperative Library Services (WCCLS) and the Washington\nCounty Broadba
 nd Action Team. The DNP is funded in part by American Connections\nCorps\,
  an AmeriCorps program dedicated to advancing economic prosperity by bridg
 ing\nthe digital divide. This project is being supported\, in part\, by fe
 deral award number\nSLFRP0228 awarded to Washington County by the U.S. Dep
 artment of the Treasury.
LOCATION:Banks Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/68f17e4861706d28001e1907
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wccls Library": "https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6917a2c3886bb73600bad5be"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wccls_library
SUMMARY:Wind Down Wednesdays
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260401T170000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260401T180000Z
UID:6917a2c3886bb73600bad5be@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Start your morning off right and join us in the Rogers Room on
  the first Wednesday of every month for a free one-hour intro level class 
 designed to help manage stress and promote well-being through progressive 
 muscle relaxation\, mindfulness\, and deep breathing. Teacher Ruby offers 
 practical tips for identifying stressors in your life\, implementing simpl
 e coping mechanisms\, and cultivating emotional survival skills that focus
  on humor and creativity. Bring your own pillow and/or mat\, wear comfy cl
 othes\, and prepare to fully unwind.\nThis class is open to adults 16 year
 s or older\, but registration is required\, and enrollment is limited to 2
 0 people.
LOCATION:Forest Grove City Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6917a2c3886bb73600bad5be
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
