  designed to teach the basics and help you become proficient in using comp
 uters\, office software\, browsing the internet\, sending emails\, and mor
 e.\n¡Ven y da el primer paso para dominar la tecnología! Nuestra clase e
 stá diseñada para aprender los conceptos básicos y ayudarte a dominar e
 l uso de computadoras\, software de oficina\, navegar por Internet\, envia
 r correos electrónicos y más.
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6998e4728b29ea2800d17374
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wccls Library": "https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69adfdd34dacf581ff80841b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wccls_library
SUMMARY:Truth and AI: Misinformation\, Deepfakes\, and the Digital World
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260403T010000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260403T020000Z
UID:69adfdd34dacf581ff80841b@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI can create photos\, videos\, and stories that look real but
  aren’t\, so how do you know what’s real online anymore? Learn how the
 se tricks work\, why they spread so quickly\, and practice spotting the si
 gns of misinformation before it fools you. This session will help you shar
 pen your skills to recognize misleading content\, understand how deepfakes
  are made\, and learn practical strategies for separating fact from fictio
 n in your daily digital life.\nRegistration is encouraged\, but not requir
 ed.\nPresenter Bio:\nCrystal Trice has over 20 years of experience in libr
 aries and education and is the founder of\nScissors & Glue\, LLC\n. She le
 ads interactive trainings and workshops on topics ranging from project man
 agement to artificial intelligence\, helping libraries and schools spark p
 ositive change. Based near Portland\, Oregon\, Crystal enjoys life with he
 r husband\, a small menagerie of farm animals\, and an endless supply of s
 ticky notes and colorful pens.
LOCATION:Sherwood Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69adfdd34dacf581ff80841b
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Japanese Garden": "https://japanesegarden.org/events/member-extended-hours-2026-04-02/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:japanese_garden
X-SOURCE:Japanese Garden
UID:5295@japanesegarden.org
DTSTART:20260403T013000Z
DTEND:20260403T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20260309T091956Z
URL:https://japanesegarden.org/events/member-extended-hours-2026-04-02/
SUMMARY:Member Extended Hours
DESCRIPTION:[caption id="attachment_5922" align="alignnone" width="788"] Photo by Jonathan Ley[/caption]\n\nAs the sun begins to set and the daily crowds depart\, we invite our members and their guests to experience the Garden in one of its most tranquil states. During these exclusive extended hours\, you can enjoy a peaceful stroll through the winding paths\, taking in the shifting light and evening serenity that few get to witness.\n\nFor safety reasons\, the Natural Garden may be closed early.\n\nMembers are always welcome to bring guests during any Member Hours. If any guests are not covered by the membership for free\, extra tickets can be purchased at check-in. Members always receive a 20% discount on any general admission tickets.  
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://wpmedia.japanesegarden.org/w:1600/h:1067/q:mauto/process:5922/id:15238728a99f6d3b14a6b18fb2f3b7ba/https://japanesegarden.org/Twilight-Hours-071317-image-050-1.jpg
CATEGORIES:Member Only,Special Events
LOCATION:Portland Japanese Garden\, 611 SW Kingston Ave.\, Portland\, OR\, 97205\, United States
GEO:45.51862;-122.70843109999998
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=611 SW Kingston Ave.\, Portland\, OR\, 97205\, United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Portland Japanese Garden:geo:45.51862;-122.70843109999998
END:VEVENT
