SUMMARY:We Belong! Rethinking How We Teach Disability Focusing on Assets\,
  Identity\, and What It Means to Be Human
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260411T160000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260411T180000Z
UID:688be1156d83b22800db441a@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:How teachers characterize the experiences of disabled people f
 orm the foundation of children's knowledge and beliefs\, often this perspe
 ctive is centered on weaknesses or deficits. In this training participants
  will implement a strengths-based view of the foundational beliefs about a
 nd responses to disability\, casting it as another variation of what it me
 ans to be a human focus viewing human.\nCKC: SN | 2 hours | Set One | ARC
 : IT\nTrainer: Kelley Lawson\nThis childcare provider training is hosted 
 by Cedar Mill & Bethany Community Libraries.
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/688be1156d83b22800db441a
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
