X-SOURCE-ID:wccls_library
SUMMARY:English for Speakers of Other Languages / Inglés para hablantes d
 e otros idiomas
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T230000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260417T000000Z
UID:69af502e4a9fd98b7f8335cc@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Inglés para hablantes de otros idiomas\, clase de nivel inici
 al\, los jueves de 4:00 a 5:00 p. m. en la biblioteca\nGoodwill Industries
  está ofreciendo clases de inglés gratuitas para personas que hablan otr
 os idiomas. Esta clase es una introducción a habilidades básicas de gram
 ática\, lectura\, escritura\, comprensión y expresión oral para estudia
 ntes que pueden leer y escribir en su idioma materno. Trabajaremos juntos 
 para aprender nuevo vocabulario y patrones oracionales\, así también com
 o a comunicarse utilizando un inglés sencillo. No es necesario inscribirs
 e.\nEnglish for Speakers of Other Languages Beginning Level Class Thursday
 s from 4:00-5:00p.m. in the library\nGoodwill Industries is offering free 
 English classes for speakers of other languages. This class is an introduc
 tion to basic grammar\, reading\, writing\, listening\, and speaking skill
 s. We will work together to learn new vocabulary\, sentence patterns\, and
  communication using simple English. Registration is not required.
LOCATION:North Plains Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69af502e4a9fd98b7f8335cc
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wccls Library": "https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f9fb58b29ea2800d28bc9"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wccls_library
SUMMARY:Makerspace Open Lab
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260416T230000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260417T010000Z
UID:699f9fb58b29ea2800d28bc9@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Makerspace Open Labs are for anyone who wants to check out the
  space and use our equipment to make cool things. Room assistants are avai
 lable to guide you in the basic use of the tools and technology. Come in w
 ith an idea and leave with a finished project! For more information about 
 the Makerspace and its resources\,\nsee here\n.\nMakerspace Open Labs take
  place on the following weekly schedule:\nTuesdays\n\, 5:30 - 7:30PM\nThur
 sdays\n\, 4:00 - 6:00PM\nSaturdays\n\, 10:00 AM - 1:00PM\nSundays\n\, 1:30
  - 5:30P\nEach month we provide the materials\, tools and instructions for
  a featured Makerspace project that everyone is invited to try.\nApril's f
 eatured project is Seed Paper bookmarks (pictured).\nIMPORTANT:\nAdults us
 ing the Makerspace for the first time need to\nsign a waiver\n\; people un
 der the age of 18 must have a waiver signed by a parent or guardian.\nYou 
 can sign and submit waivers online here.
LOCATION:Tualatin Public Library\, Makerspace
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f9fb58b29ea2800d28bc9
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Portland Community College": "https://events.pcc.edu/event/10023-ekphrasis-a-pcc-district-wide-faculty-exhibition"}
X-SOURCE-ID:portland_community_college
X-SOURCE:Portland Community College
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260417
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260418
SUMMARY:Ekphrasis: A PCC District-Wide Faculty Exhibition
DESCRIPTION:Exhibition Dates: February 26\, 2026 – April 17\, 2026Galle
 ry hours: Monday – Friday\, 8am-4pm.Opening Reception: Saturday\, Febru
 ary 28\, 5:00 – 8:00 p.m.Additional Events announced soon.Ekphrasis com
 es from the Greek words ek (out) and phrásis (speak)\, literally speakin
 g out. The Poetry Foundation defines an ekphrastic poem as a vivid descri
 ption of a work of art. But ekphrasis is more than giving voice to the vi
 sual\, more than mere description. Ekphrasis offers one's voice in dialog
 ue with another. In Ekphrasis: A PCC Faculty Exhibition\, recent art from
  Portland Community College art faculty and lab techs is positioned in co
 nversation\, both with each other and with writing faculty who composed e
 kphrastic poems about the work.—Event Details: https://hub.pcc.edu/rsvp
 ?id=382395 (https://hub.pcc.edu/rsvp?id=382395)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Exhibition Dates: February 26\, 2026 – Apr
 il 17\, 2026<br />Gallery hours: Monday – Friday\, 8am-4pm.<br />Openin
 g Reception: Saturday\, February 28\, 5:00 – 8:00 p.m.<br />Additional 
 Events announced soon.<br />Ekphrasis comes from the Greek words ek (out)
  and phrásis (speak)\, literally speaking out. The Poetry Foundation def
 ines an ekphrastic poem as a vivid description of a work of art. But ekph
 rasis is more than giving voice to the visual\, more than mere descriptio
 n. Ekphrasis offers one's voice in dialogue with another. In Ekphrasis: A
  PCC Faculty Exhibition\, recent art from Portland Community College art 
 faculty and lab techs is positioned in conversation\, both with each othe
 r and with writing faculty who composed ekphrastic poems about the work.<
 br />—<br />Event Details: <a href="https://hub.pcc.edu/rsvp?id=382395"
  target="_blank">https://hub.pcc.edu/rsvp?id=382395</a>
UID:20260417T070000Z-10023@events.pcc.edu
DTSTAMP:20260219T185839Z
URL:https://events.pcc.edu/event/10023-ekphrasis-a-pcc-district-wide-facu
 lty-exhibition
