SUMMARY:Read to the Dogs/Lee a los perros
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260423T230000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260423T233000Z
UID:6932400b94297d36009e5b0f@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Want to build your skills and confidence? Read aloud to a trai
 ned therapy dog (accompanied by their handler) in a private 20-minute sess
 ion. Grades K – 12.\n¿Quieres mejorar tus habilidades y tu confianza? I
 nscríbete para leer en voz alta a perros de terapia (acompañados por un 
 entrenador) en una sesión privada de 20 minutos. K – 12o grado.\nYou ma
 y sign up for one(1) Read to the Dogs session within a one(1) month period
 .
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Brookwood
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6932400b94297d36009e5b0f
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wccls Library": "https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69af502e4a9fd98b7f8335cd"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wccls_library
SUMMARY:English for Speakers of Other Languages / Inglés para hablantes d
 e otros idiomas
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260423T230000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260424T000000Z
UID:69af502e4a9fd98b7f8335cd@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Inglés para hablantes de otros idiomas\, clase de nivel inici
 al\, los jueves de 4:00 a 5:00 p. m. en la biblioteca\nGoodwill Industries
  está ofreciendo clases de inglés gratuitas para personas que hablan otr
 os idiomas. Esta clase es una introducción a habilidades básicas de gram
 ática\, lectura\, escritura\, comprensión y expresión oral para estudia
 ntes que pueden leer y escribir en su idioma materno. Trabajaremos juntos 
 para aprender nuevo vocabulario y patrones oracionales\, así también com
 o a comunicarse utilizando un inglés sencillo. No es necesario inscribirs
 e.\nEnglish for Speakers of Other Languages Beginning Level Class Thursday
 s from 4:00-5:00p.m. in the library\nGoodwill Industries is offering free 
 English classes for speakers of other languages. This class is an introduc
 tion to basic grammar\, reading\, writing\, listening\, and speaking skill
 s. We will work together to learn new vocabulary\, sentence patterns\, and
  communication using simple English. Registration is not required.
LOCATION:North Plains Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69af502e4a9fd98b7f8335cd
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wccls Library": "https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f9fb58b29ea2800d28bcd"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wccls_library
SUMMARY:Makerspace Open Lab
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260423T230000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260424T010000Z
UID:699f9fb58b29ea2800d28bcd@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Makerspace Open Labs are for anyone who wants to check out the
  space and use our equipment to make cool things. Room assistants are avai
 lable to guide you in the basic use of the tools and technology. Come in w
 ith an idea and leave with a finished project! For more information about 
 the Makerspace and its resources\,\nsee here\n.\nMakerspace Open Labs take
  place on the following weekly schedule:\nTuesdays\n\, 5:30 - 7:30PM\nThur
 sdays\n\, 4:00 - 6:00PM\nSaturdays\n\, 10:00 AM - 1:00PM\nSundays\n\, 1:30
  - 5:30P\nEach month we provide the materials\, tools and instructions for
  a featured Makerspace project that everyone is invited to try.\nApril's f
 eatured project is Seed Paper bookmarks (pictured).\nIMPORTANT:\nAdults us
 ing the Makerspace for the first time need to\nsign a waiver\n\; people un
 der the age of 18 must have a waiver signed by a parent or guardian.\nYou 
 can sign and submit waivers online here.
LOCATION:Tualatin Public Library\, Makerspace
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f9fb58b29ea2800d28bcd
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
