BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:friends_of_trees_green_space
X-SOURCE:Friends Of Trees Green Space
DTSTART:20260425T164500Z
DTEND:20260425T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T060605Z
UID:3lnsv1bheagsc4i8hrk3lnp4h8@google.com
CREATED:20260123T232520Z
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Earth Week by mulching hundreds of native pollinator-
 friendly species at Wilkes Creek Headwaters! We may also take out some weed
 y introduced plants\, if time allows. <u>Note: there will be no tree-planti
 ng at this event\, and this can be physically-demanding work</u> (great for
  folks looking for a work out!).  Our stewardship events help to ensure the
  highest level of plant survival through the PNW dry summer months ahead.<b
 r><p><b>How do I register? </b>Register by filling out <b><a href="https://
 www.tfaforms.com/4840511?tfa_26=a0TPa00001Edi8m&tfa_2189=Wilkes%20Creek%20H
 eadwaters%20Stewardship\,%20NE%20Portland&tfa_31=a0VPa00000DfdEJ&tfa_45=%20
 at%20April%2025\,%202026%20at%209:45%20am&tfa_2190=2026-04-25&tfa_49=3.25&t
 fa_886=Portland%20Parks%20and%20Recreation&tfa_51=offsite" target="_blank">
 <u><u><u><u><u><u>this quick form</u></u></u></u></u></u></a></b>.  Groups\
 , families\, and individuals welcome!</p><u></u><p><b>Please arrive by 9:45
 am</b> to find our tent and sign-in\, stewardship activities start promptly
  at 10:00am. We provide gloves\, tools\, and guidance. All you need to do i
 s show up dressed for the weather and wearing sturdy shoes or boots (no san
 dals of any kind\, please!) and be ready to have fun!</p><p><b>Under age 18
 ?</b> We request that youth 15 and under volunteer with a parent/guardian. 
  Youth 16 and older can volunteer on their own and will need to hand us a <
 b><a href="https://friendsoftrees.org/youthwaiver" target="_blank"><u><u><u
 ><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>youth waiver form</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u><
 /u></u></u></a></b> signed by their parent/guardian.</p><p><b>Questions?  <
 /b>Pl<u></u>ease check out our <a href="https://friendsoftrees.org/voluntee
 r-faq/" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><b><u>Volunt
 eer FAQ webpage</u></b></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u>
 </a>.  Our team is also happy to assist! <a href="mailto:Volunteer@friendso
 ftrees.org" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><b><u>vo
 lunteer@fr<u></u>iendsoftrees.or<u></u>g</u></b></u></u></u></u></u></u></u
 ></u></u></u></u></u></u></a> / 503-595-0213 We look forward to working tog
 ether soon!</p><hr /><p>This event is in partnership with Portland Parks &a
 mp\; Recreation and Portland OIC.</p>
