 ing="lazy" data-optimized="true"/></picture> Krystal Marcinkiewicz\, MA\,
  LPC\, LMHC is a Licensed Professional Counselor and Clinical Supervisor\
 , having earned her Masters Degree in Professional Mental Health Counseli
 ng from Lewis &amp\; Clark College in 2018. Drawing from an integrative f
 eminist approach\, her work is grounded in person-centered values\, empha
 sizing authentic connection\, and collaborative engagement. Her primary c
 linical focus is supporting clients in navigating identity development\, 
 body politics\, neurodivergence\, emotional codependency\, highly sensiti
 ve personalities and other complex emotional experiences.</p><p style="li
 ne-height: 1.6\;">  In addition to clinical work\, Krystal is also passio
 nate in training and mentoring emerging counselors. She is an adjunct pro
 fessor\, teaching a wide variety of graduate counseling courses with an u
 nderlying emphasis on counselor identity development\, reflective practic
 e\, and cultivating professional resilience.</p><p style="line-height: 1.
 6\;">  In both the classroom\, and her clinical work\, Krystal is committ
 ed to creating affirming spaces that honor intersectional identities and 
 lived experience.</p><div id="lw_widget_470b39ba" class="lw_widget lw_wid
